### 2. src/features/meetings/MeetingActiveHeader.tsx:41-42
BEFORE: `<span className="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full spectral-active animate-pulse" aria-hidden="true" />` (spectral + indefinite pulse, §10 violation)
AFTER:  `<span className="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-error" aria-hidden="true" />` (live red, no animation)
Comment updated: `§14.12 — meeting dot uses error/live red, not spectral; no indefinite pulse (§10)`
Token: `bg-error` → `--color-error` → `--md-error` (verified src/index.css:59,262,379)
Spec §14.12 verbatim: "the meeting dot uses `error`/live red, not spectral". The live red color signals activity; the redundant `animate-pulse` is the §10 violation and is removed.
Single round element, no animation, no spectral.

### 3. src/design-system/components/Progress.tsx:47
BEFORE: `after:animate-[spectral-sweep_800ms_linear_infinite]` (infinite spectral pulse, §10 violation)
AFTER:  `after:animate-[spectral-sweep_800ms_ease-out_1] motion-reduce:after:animate-none` (one-time sweep, gated for prefers-reduced-motion)
Spec §10: "Project Pulse travels the gradient once per progress change, then stops" — same rule applied here.
Easing is `ease-out` (M3 default for completed transitions), duration 800ms unchanged (existing token budget), count `_1` = 1 iteration. `motion-reduce:after:animate-none` preserves the existing accessibility behavior.
Existing `bg-primary` fill remains the visible track — no hex/px added.

